  "name": "LE Cells",
  "code": "LE CELLS",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>The LE Cells test is a laboratory test used to help diagnose systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE), an autoimmune disease that can affect multiple organs and tissues in the body. During this test, a blood sample is examined under a microscope to look for white blood cells with a characteristic \"leopard spot\" appearance.<br></p><p>The presence of LE cells may suggest the possibility of SLE or other autoimmune diseases, but a positive result alone is not enough to make a definitive diagnosis. Other clinical and laboratory factors must also be considered.<br></p>",
